  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plus-plus",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"assets/logo.svg\" width=\"96\" alt=\"dsh-plus-plus\"></p>\n\n**DSH++ — a local-first control plane for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (`dsh`).**\n\nIt runs on your machine, reads the same `$DSH_HOME` state the harness does, and gives you the operational layer the harness doesn't ship.\n\n**Why you need it**"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plus-plus",
      "text": "- You can't easily see which plugins are installed, or what each one can reach (filesystem, shell, network, credentials).\n- A config change, a new plugin, a prompt tweak, or a harness upgrade can silently break a workflow — and you only find out later.\n- Credentials, config, and sessions live in `$DSH_HOME` with no snapshot/rollback or usage/cost view.\n\n**Core capabilities**"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plus-plus",
      "text": "1. **Plugin security auditing** — `dshpp audit` inventories installed plugins, classifies the capabilities (seams) each one touches, grades risk, and flags what to remove.\n2. **Workflow regression testing** — `dshpp test` runs a fixed set of harness tasks against your current DSH configuration, compares to a stored baseline, and reports regressions. It exits non-zero on a regression, so it can gate CI.\n3. **Lifecycle management** — detect the install, snapshot and roll back `$DSH_HOME` configuration, run diagnostics, and manage providers and credentials."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plus-plus",
      "text": "**Install & go**\n\n```sh\nnpm i -g .\ndshpp status   # overview of the DSH install\ndshpp audit    # plugin security risk report\ndshpp test     # regression-test the DSH workflow vs baseline"
    },
    {
      "section": "Demo",
      "text": "Change a DSH workflow, run `dshpp test`, and it finds the regression:\n\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"assets/demo-regression.gif\" width=\"760\" alt=\"dshpp test after changing the DSH workflow finds a regression\"></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js >= 20.\n- No third-party runtime dependencies. Built-in `node:zlib` decodes the concatenated-zstd session logs."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm i -g .\n```\n\nOr install it as a harness plugin (adds a `/dshpp` slash command):\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:limlnx523/dsh-plus-plus\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Example",
      "text": "```text\n$ dshpp status\n\n[DSH++] DeepSeek Harness · status\n----------------------------------------------------"
    },
    {
      "section": "CLI",
      "text": "```text\ndshpp status                      Overview (home, env, settings, backups)\ndshpp doctor                      Diagnostics checklist\ndshpp env ls [--show]             List credentials (masked unless --show)\ndshpp env set KEY=VALUE           Add/update a credential"
    },
    {
      "section": "Web console",
      "text": "`dshpp web` serves a local console at `http://127.0.0.1:4848/`. It binds to loopback only. It surfaces providers, masked credentials, backups, usage and cost, sessions, plugins, and regression results. Secrets are masked unless you opt in with `--show`, and the console never returns raw key values over the API."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "- Harness home: `$DSH_HOME` or `~/.dsh`\n- Credentials: `$DSH_HOME/.env` (never committed; snapshots warn when they include it)\n- dsh-plus-plus state: `~/.dsh-plus-plus/` (backups, provider manifest, regression baseline)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm link\nnode bin/dshpp.mjs --help\nnpm test\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
